  "id": "two-tailed-test",
  "term": "two-tailed test",
  "definition": "A two-tailed test is a significance test that looks at outcomes in both directions from the value expected under the null hypothesis. It asks how likely it is to obtain a result at least as far from that value as the observed one, whether the statistic is higher or lower.",
